# Policy Test Case Authoring Rules

Policy test cases validate CEL and AI rules in Maybe Don't. Tests are organized in a suite directory with `suite.yaml` and test case files in `cases/`.

## Required Structure

```
suite-dir/
  suite.yaml          # Suite configuration
  cases/
    *.yaml            # Test case files (single or array format)
```

## Rules

1. Every test case MUST have a unique `case_id` across the entire suite
2. Use descriptive kebab-case IDs with engine and phase prefix: `cel-req-001`, `ai-resp-redact-pii`
3. `request` is required when `phase` includes `request`; `response` is required when `phase` includes `response`
4. `expectations.decision` is REQUIRED and must be one of: `allow`, `deny`, `redact`
5. For redact tests, provide `expectations.redacted_content` with the expected output
6. Tag cases consistently for filtering: `cel`, `ai`, `request`, `response`, `deny`, `allow`, `redact`
7. Write both allow and deny tests for each policy rule

## Test Case Structure

```yaml
- case_id: "cel-req-001"
  title: "Block delete_file"
  tags: [cel, request, github]
  notes: ["Tests exact name matching"]
  phase: request                      # request, response, both
  engine: cel                         # cel, ai, both
  request:
    tool_name: "github__delete_file"
    arguments: {owner: "org"}
  response:                           # Required when phase includes response
    content:
      - type: text
        text: "Content here"
    is_error: false
  expectations:
    decision: deny
    policies:
      - policy_name: "deny-delete-file"
        decision: deny
    redacted_content:                 # For redact tests only
      - type: text
        text: "[REDACTED]"
```

## Suite Configuration

```yaml
version: "v1"
bundle_id: "my-suite"
policies:
  cel_request_rules: "../cel_request_rules.yaml"
  ai_request_rules: "../ai_request_rules.yaml"
providers:
  openai:
    api_key: "${OPENAI_API_KEY}"
acceptance:
  min_match_rate: 1.0
  strict_policy_match: true
engines:
  cel:
    enabled: true
  ai:
    enabled: true
    model_matrix:
      - provider: openai
        model: gpt-5-mini
```

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all tests
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests

# CEL only
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests --engine cel

# Single AI model
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests --model openai:gpt-5-mini

# Filter by tags
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests --tags cel,request

# Incremental (skip unchanged)
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests --incremental

# Retry failures
maybe-dont test policies --suite-dir ./tests --incremental --retry-failed
```

## Exit Codes

- `0` — All passed
- `1` — Test failure
- `2` — Schema validation error
- `3` — Policy integrity error
- `4` — Path resolution error
- `5` — More tests remain (`--max-tests`)
